hi Giancarlo,
you would expect some singular hessian errors in doing this, which is ok. That is just telling you that the parameter space is lower-dimensional then the parameter vector you're feeding optim() -- which is true in this particular case.
It wouldn't surprise me that the SE(p) is large, but that number is meaningless in the context (as p-> boundary of the parameter space). The other ones should be good.
I think this approach is fine.

regards
andy

